From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python: Tcl's library for the interpreter Tech() makes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Bazel build embeds Tcl's library scripts (init.tcl and friends) in a
zip that the openroad binary mounts in main() before Tcl_Init
(in_bazel::SetupTclEnvironment). The Python bindings' Tech() creates its
interpreter and runs Tcl_Init without it, so init.tcl is never read and
what it defines is missing: ORFS's load.tcl and every script that calls
`clock` fail with

  Ambiguous command name "clock": clock_gating clock_tree_synthesis.

ord_py.tcl_library_init() mounts the library for the current OpenROAD's
interpreter and runs Tcl_Init again. It is in the Python wrapper only, so
the openroad binary and everything keyed on it are unchanged.

Not upstreamed. Retires on the //:bump onto an OpenROAD whose Python
bindings initialise Tcl's library themselves.
---
diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index e51f604e..11f7c745 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -437,7 +437,9 @@ python_wrap_library(
     deps = [
         ":openroad_lib",
         ":ord",
+        "//bazel:tcl_library_init",
         "//src/ifp",
+        "@tcl_lang//:tcl",
     ],
 )
 
diff --git a/src/OpenRoad-py.i b/src/OpenRoad-py.i
index 54d6d567..cfb9b8f6 100644
--- a/src/OpenRoad-py.i
+++ b/src/OpenRoad-py.i
@@ -68,6 +68,27 @@ get_db_block();
 #ifdef BAZEL
 %import "src/odb/src/swig/common/odb.i"
 %import "src/utl/src/Logger-py.i"
+
+%{
+#include "bazel/tcl_library_init.h"
+#include "ord/OpenRoad.hh"
+#include "tcl.h"
+%}
+
+%inline %{
+// Tech() runs Tcl_Init on an interpreter that has no library: a Bazel
+// build embeds Tcl's library scripts in a zip the openroad binary mounts
+// in main() (SetupTclEnvironment), and nothing mounts it for Python, so
+// init.tcl and what it defines (clock, among others) are missing. Mounts
+// it for the current OpenROAD's interpreter and runs Tcl_Init again;
+// true when both succeed.
+bool tcl_library_init()
+{
+  Tcl_Interp* interp = ord::OpenRoad::openRoad()->tclInterp();
+  return in_bazel::SetupTclEnvironment(interp) == TCL_OK
+         && Tcl_Init(interp) == TCL_OK;
+}
+%}
 #endif
 
 %newobject Design::getFloorplan();
